{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>For, etc.</b> It is possible that this pericope is an interpretation of the cedars and the mountains and all of them, or it is possible that it is joined with \"he has ceased for you from man,\" and this is the correct view in my eyes." "<b>Support and stay.</b> A figure of speech, and the sense is every support, and it means every support of bread and water."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:51:44.975462780Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}